<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container dbb-copy">
        <h2>Reconnect with Your Body</h2>
        <p>Dynamic Body Balancing (DBB) is a gentle bodywork approach that combines fascial release, craniosacral techniques, and energy-based practices to support relaxation, body awareness, and a sense of balance.</p>
        <p>Your body responds to the many demands of everyday life, including physical tension, stress, and emotional experiences. DBB uses gentle touch, subtle movement, and mindful awareness to explore areas of tension and encourage the body to soften and release.</p>
        <p>Sessions are performed fully clothed and may involve sitting, standing, or lying down, depending on the techniques used and your individual needs.</p>
        <p>The experience is an opportunity to slow down and tune into your body. As you become more aware of your physical and emotional responses, you may notice spontaneous movement, including movements that resemble how your body responded during a past accident or physical experience. Some people may also experience emotional release or a sense of stress and tension releasing. These responses can vary from person to person, and you are encouraged to move at your own pace, with support and attention to your comfort and boundaries.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section alt">
    <div class="container dbb-copy">
        <h2>Terminology</h2>
        <h3>Fascial Release</h3>
        <p>Fascia is the connective tissue that surrounds and supports your muscles, organs, nerves, and other structures throughout your body. DBB uses gentle touch and guided movement to explore areas of restriction and encourage greater ease of movement.</p>
        <h3>Craniosacral Techniques</h3>
        <p>Craniosacral therapy involves gentle, hands-on techniques focused around the head, spine, and sacrum (the triangular bone at the base of the spine). These techniques are intended to support and balance the natureal flow of cerbrospinal fluid.</p>
        <h3>Energy-Based Practices</h3>
        <p>DBB incorporates biofield approaches, which work with the concept of the body's subtle energy field. These practices may involve gentle touch, focused attention, and awareness of the body's responses to support a feeling of balance and connection.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container dbb-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">What happens during a session?</span>
        <h2>What to Expect</h2>
        <p>Every Dynamic Body Balancing session is guided by your individual needs and comfort level.</p>
        <ul class="dbb-list">
            <li><strong>You remain fully clothed.</strong> Wear comfortable clothes that allow you to move easily.</li>
            <li><strong>Gentle, intentional touch.</strong> Techniques may involve light hands-on contact or subtle guided movement.</li>
            <li><strong>You may sit, stand, or lie down.</strong> Your position depends on the techniques being used and what feels appropriate for you.</li>
            <li><strong>Your body may be guided into intuitive movement.</strong> With the facilitator's gentle guidance and support, you may be invited to allow your body to move in its own way. Rather than following a prescribed sequence, you listen to your body's natural impulses and move with your body as it responds.</li>
            <li><strong>You are encouraged to notice what you feel.</strong> You may be invited to breathe naturally, relax, and pay attention to sensations, areas of tension, or the movements that arise. The facilitator helps guide the process, while your body leads the movement.</li>
            <li><strong>Your experience is your own.</strong> Some people experience deep relaxation, while others notice changes in body awareness, movement, or emotional responses. Experiences vary, and there is no right or wrong way to respond.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="dbb-note">Your comfort, boundaries, and consent remain important throughout the session.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section alt">
    <div class="container dbb-copy">
        <h2>Is Dynamic Body Balancing Right for You?</h2>
        <p>You may be interested in exploring Dynamic Body Balancing if you would like to:</p>
        <ul class="dbb-list">
            <li>Find time to slow down and relax.</li>
            <li>Become more aware of tension and holding patterns in your body.</li>
            <li>Explore gentle approaches to movement and body awareness.</li>
            <li>Create space to reconnect with yourself during stressful seasons of life.</li>
            <li>Experience a holistic approach that considers the relationship between physical sensations, emotional experiences, and overall well-being.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="dbb-note">You don't need prior experience with bodywork or energy practices. An open mind and a willingness to notice your body's responses are enough to begin. Dynamic Body Balancing is a complementary wellness practice, not a substitute for medical evaluation, diagnosis, or treatment.</p>
    </div>
</section>

